WHAT ADDING A HYPOTHESIS PROVIDER COSTS
==========================================================================
  adapter modules registered: 1
    app/ai/providers/template.py  27 lines of code

  ...and everywhere else:
    app/ai/registry.py       1 import line(s) and 1 mapping entry(ies) for 1 provider(s)
    app/ai/service.py        0 -- the interface imports no adapter
    every caller             0 -- a caller is handed a generator and cannot tell which

  So one provider = 1 new module + 2 lines in 1 existing file,
  and 0 changes anywhere else.

  CAVEAT, and it matters: the shipped adapter wraps a local function and
  makes no network call, so its own size is a LOWER BOUND -- a hosted
  adapter will be several times larger. The claim is about the cost
  OUTSIDE the new module, and that cost does not depend on what the
  adapter does.

  For comparison, the interface it plugs into:
    app/ai/service.py     121 lines of code
    app/ai/registry.py    24 lines of code
